BEGIN:VEVENT
DURATION:PT5H
LOCATION:Staff Club then E7A 333
DTSTAMP:20071204T012547Z
UID:0806F75C-BB4E-4FED-B703-2B9FD8871511
SEQUENCE:36
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20071205T124500
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20071205T124500
SUMMARY:Category Seminar
DESCRIPTION:At 3:45pm\n\nSpeaker:  Jon Cohen (Macquarie/ANU)\n\nTitle:  
 \"Coherent presentations of structural monoids.\"\n\nAbstract: In a seri
 es of papers\, P. Dehornoy has investigated certain algebraic invariants
  associated with balanced equational varieties. In general\, these invar
 iants form inverse monoids\, known as \"structural monoids\"\, but parti
 cularly nice cases result in groups. Dehornoy has shown that Richard Tho
 mpson's groups F and V\, each of which is finitely presentable\, infinit
 e and simple\, arise as the invariants associated to the varieties of se
 migroups and of commutative semigroups\, respectively. He subsequently o
 btained presentations of these groups utilising the pentagon and hexagon
  coherence axioms for coherently associative and commutative bifunctors.
  This talk will show how to systematise this observation. To every balan
 ced equational variety E\, we will associate a collection of categorific
 ations. Each categorification yields a presentation of an inverse monoid
 \, which is isomorphic to the structural monoid of E if and only if the 
 categorification is coherent. The resulting presentations reflect some n
 ice combinatorial features of the structural monoids. We may also briefl
 y see how to extend this construction to any rewriting 2-theory\, which 
 is a Cat-enriched Lawvere theory definable by variables\, with the level
  of detail being proportional to the time until drinks...\n\n\n---------
 ------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ---\nWe will have lunch in the Macquarie Staff Club. We leave from E7A L
 evel 3 at 12.45 pm.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DURATION:PT5H
LOCATION:Central Coast
DTSTAMP:20080110T001543Z
UID:0806F75C-BB4E-4FED-B703-2B9FD8871511
SEQUENCE:40
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20080109T124500
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20080109T124500
SUMMARY:Woods Outing
DESCRIPTION:Maitland Bay\nGosford Gallery
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
LOCATION:Staff Club then E7A 333
DTSTAMP:20080110T063228Z
UID:0806F75C-BB4E-4FED-B703-2B9FD8871511
SEQUENCE:42
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20080116T124500
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20080116T154500
SUMMARY:Category Seminar
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20080116T170000
DESCRIPTION:Speaker:  Richard Wood (Dalhouse)\n\nTitle:  \"Frobenius Obj
 ects in Cartesian Bicategories\" joint work with Bob Walters.\n\nAbstrac
 t: \nIn recent joint work\, Bob Walters and the speaker have shown that\
 nmaps (left adjoint arrows) between Frobenius objects in a cartesian\nbi
 category ${\\bf B}$ are precisely comonoid homomorphisms and\, for\n$A$ 
 Frobenius and any $T$ in ${\\bf B}$\, ${\\rm map}({\\bf B})(T\,A)$\nis a
  groupoid.\n\nIn this talk\, the context of the second result will be th
 oroughly\nexplained and a proof given. As a corollary\, it follows that 
 a\nFrobenius object in the bicategory of categories and profunctors is\n
 a groupoid. This last result was first proved about 20 years ago by\nAur
 elio Carboni and the speaker\, independently. However\, it is only\nrece
 ntly that generalian bicategories have been defined so as to be\nable to
  contemplate the present theorem.\n
END:VEVENT
