BEGIN:VEVENT
DURATION:PT1H
LOCATION:E4A\, 523 (level 5 seminar room)
DTSTAMP:20060901T060006Z
UID:7B468EC3-81AE-479C-BF02-6AABFFA1666A
SEQUENCE:5
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20060905T140000
SUMMARY:Talk on Quizzes
DESCRIPTION:Speakers: Fran Griffin\, Department of Mathematics\, Macquar
 ie\nUniversity.\nand Sibba Gudlaugsdottir\, Department of Statistics\, M
 acquarie\nUniversity.\n\nTitle: Using online quizzes to boost performanc
 e in STAT279 and in\n100-level mathematics.\n\nAbstract: Online quizzes 
 have been developed and used for several\nyears in the Department of Mat
 hematics\, and have recently been\nadopted by the Department of Statisti
 cs for use in STAT279. In this\nunit\, the online quizzes have replaced 
 paper based quizzes\, and have\nbecome a learning tool for the students 
 rather than simply a way to\nassess their progress.\n\nThe MacQTeX quizz
 es are presented as interactive PDF documents\, and\nare available onlin
 e 24 hours a day for students. The question types\ninclude multiple choi
 ce\, multiple response and fill-in-the-answer.\nThe last accepts numeric
 \, text or mathematical expressions as input\,\nand recognises equivalen
 t expressions. Various parameters in the\nquestions are randomised\, so 
 that students may attempt many versions\nof the same quiz\, gaining valu
 able practice. On completion of a quiz\,\n\nit is marked and fully worke
 d solutions become available\, giving\nstudents immediate feedback.\n\nW
 e will demonstrate the quizzes and the quiz management tools\, and\ndesc
 ribe how the MacQTeX system works. The affect on students and\ntheir rea
 ction to the quizzes will be discussed\, along with\neducational issues 
 related to the level of randomisation in the\nquestions.\n
END:VEVENT
