BEGIN:VEVENT
DURATION:PT1H
LOCATION:E7B263
DTSTAMP:20070321T063912Z
UID:D35DC9D2-66E4-4BC1-8D45-508892AF5A77
SEQUENCE:8
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20070326T130000
SUMMARY:Colloquium
DESCRIPTION:Mathematics Colloquium\n\nMon 26 March  at 1 pm  in E7B263\n
 \nTitle: Random walks and functional analysis methods\n\nSpeaker: Nick D
 ungey\nMacquarie\n\nAbstract.\nThe idea of a `random walk' on a space is
  one of the basic topics in probability theory. Here we discuss some app
 roaches to the analysis of random walks through ideas of functional anal
 ysis\, including the study of the powers T\, T2\, T3\, ... of a single l
 inear operator T. In the case of random walks on a group\, by using the 
 algebraic structure of the group one can obtain especially interesting r
 esults for random walks which are `centered'.\n\n-----------------------
 -------------------------------------------------\n\nWe will take the sp
 eaker out to lunch at the Staff Club.  The lunch party departs from leve
 l 4 of E7A at noon.  Please join us.
END:VEVENT
