SEQUENCE:6
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20060616
SUMMARY:Rejoinder Day
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20060617
DESCRIPTION:Rejoinder season is bearing down upon us once again: reports
  will be\navailable on GAMS on Friday (16th June)\, with a Local Submit 
 to the Research Office due by Wednesday the 28th.  Final submission by t
 he Research Office to the ARC is due on June 30th.\n\nThere is no mandat
 ory vetting of rejoinders by the Division.\nInstead\, you are strongly e
 ncouraged to seek input from your peers\,\nDepartmental research directo
 rs\, Charlotte\, and myself.\n\n\nSome suggestions for writing rejoinder
 s:\n\n1. Take a few deep breaths in and out of a paper bag.\n\n2. Show y
 our reports to your peers.  You need a detached perspective\non what the
  reports are saying and the issues you should be\naddressing.\n\n3. Use 
 statements of fact to support your arguments\, not statements of\nopinio
 n.\n\n4. Use the opportunity to bring up recent progress\, successes or\
 npublications.  Remember that your track record is a large component\nof
  the assessment.\n\n5. Show your rejoinders to your peers.  Your Departm
 ental research\ndirector\, myself and Charlotte are only too happy to of
 fer advice/comments.
END:VEVENT
