DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20071127T110000
SUMMARY:FAREWELL MORNING TEA
DESCRIPTION:Come and join us for morning tea to farewell several members
  of staff leaving us at the end of this month.\n\nWHEN - Tuesday 27/11/0
 7 @ 11 am \nWHERE - in tearoom level 4\n\nTake a break from marking etc 
 and come and join us for some exquisitely delicious cakes and tea/coffee
 .\n
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
LOCATION:Staff Club and E6A131
DTSTAMP:20080326T022044Z
UID:1AC1CA8F-0227-4FA5-B22F-FDA95959993D
SEQUENCE:6
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20080331T120000
SUMMARY:Colloquium
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20080331T140000
DESCRIPTION:Monday 31 March 2008\n\nat 1pm\n\nin E6A131\n\nSpeaker: Chri
 s Bose\,\n             Department of Mathematics and Statistics\, Univer
 sity of Victoria\, CANADA\n             (on sabbatical leave to UNSW\, J
 an-July 2008)\n\n\nTitle: Computing and approximating invariant measures
  in ergodic theory\n\n\nAbstract:  Ergodic theory is the study of measur
 able dynamical systems. In this category\, the state space is a measure 
 space X=(X\, B\, m) and the dynamics are provided by iteration of a meas
 urable mapping T:X -> X preserving the measure m (or in continuous time\
 , a measure-preserving flow). In the first half of the talk I will outli
 ne a few examples and interpret the results of ergodic theory as it rela
 tes to asymptotic behavior of the system (X\,T). Typical of such results
  are recurrence\, Birkhoff's theorem\, decay of correlations and so-on. 
 \nIn some cases\, a natural invariant measure m is known for a given map
 ping T acting on a measurable space X. In many cases m is not known. In 
 the second half of the talk we will look at a few examples and discuss h
 ow one might still infer the existence of an invariant measure m\, and h
 ow one could compute it or\, more realistically\, approximations to it.\
 n-----------------------------------------------------------------------
 -\n\nWe will take the speaker out to lunch at the Staff Club.  The lunch
  party departs from level 4 of E7A at noon.  Please join us.\n\n
END:VEVENT
