SUMMARY:Colloquium
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Douglas Rogers\n\nTitle: Cutting it fine: Euclid's 
 problem of slicing the circle.\n\nAbstract:\nA perambulation on Euclid's
  problem of drawing parallel chords of a given circle that cut off betwe
 en them one third of the area of the circle. \nFor more details\, ask Ge
 rry Myerson for a copy of the file Slices.pdf\n\nMathematics Colloquia \
 n  Friday 23 November 2007\n  at 1 pm \n  in C5C  room 498  \n \nSpeaker
 : Douglas Rogers\n\nTitle: Cutting it fine: Euclid's problem of slicing 
 the circle.\n\nAbstract:\nA perambulation on Euclid's problem of drawing
  parallel chords of a given circle that cut off between them one third o
 f the area of the circle. \n         For more details\, click the link t
 o the paper.
