DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20070907
SUMMARY:APEC Summit induced Public Holiday
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20070908
DESCRIPTION:Public Holiday Declared- Friday 7 September 2007\n\nAll Staf
 f are advised that the NSW Government has announced a public holiday to 
 coincide with the Asia-Pacific Economic Co-operation (APEC) Summit.\n\nT
 he public holiday on Friday 7 September 2007 will apply to the Sydney\nm
 etropolitan area\, including Ryde.  A full list of local council areas\n
 affected can be found at:\n\nhttp://www.industrialrelations.nsw.gov.au/h
 olidays/apec+public+holiday.html\n\nIn accordance with the Macquarie Ent
 erprise Agreement 2006-2009\, the\nUniversity will recognise 7 September
  2007 as a declared public holiday in\nNSW. As a consequence of this dec
 ision\, it will be necessary to suspend\nteaching on that day and the Re
 gistrar will be issuing a statement to all\nstudents announcing the canc
 ellation of classes.\n\nI advise that the University will need to mainta
 in essential services such\nas Security and Information Technology.  Man
 agers/ supervisors in these\nareas are encouraged to discuss local arran
 gements with affected Staff\nMembers as early as possible.  I confirm th
 at any Staff Member who is\nrequired to work on a public holiday will be
  paid at the appropriate rate or\nprovided the opportunity to take an al
 ternative day off in lieu.\n\nPlease contact Employee Relations staff on
  ext: #9703\, #9735 or #9741 with\nany queries regarding the above.\n\nI
  hope you enjoy the extra day off.\n
END:VEVENT
