BEGIN:VEVENT
LOCATION:E7B T5
DTSTAMP:20061102T052841Z
UID:BB68C0EC-37C4-46B5-8AA6-447D07241838
SEQUENCE:7
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20061107T130000
SUMMARY:Honours Student Lectures
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20061107T150000
DESCRIPTION:please note that our honours students Paul Emanuel and Timot
 hy Schlub will be giving their final lectures on\nTuesday 7 November\, i
 n  E7BT5\, starting at 1pm.\nSpeaker: Paul Emanuel \nTitle:      \"Irreg
 ularities of Point Distribution\".  \nAbstract:  My project focuses on t
 he classical problem of discrepancy with respect to aligned rectangles i
 nside $[0\,1)2$. There will be a brief segue into large discrepancy prob
 lems\, studying the applications of Fourier transforms and probabilistic
  techniques\, along with an elegant proof of Schmidt's large discrepancy
  theorem utilising convex polygons. It will culminate in considerations 
 on the van der Corput point set of $2^s$ points\, with both an explicit 
 calculation and group theoretic considerations\, leading to Fourier-Wals
 h analysis. \n(supervisor William Chen)\n\n\nSpeaker: Timothy Schlub \nT
 itle:      \"Nonlinear Control Theory\"\nAbstract:  I will be giving a b
 rief recap on what I have said in previous lectures\, i.e. Linear and no
 nlinear control theory\, then I will speak about how the study of equili
 brium regions and feedback controls help determine the controllable stat
 es and an adequate control function.\n(supervisor Bon Clarke)
END:VEVENT
