DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20070207T090000
SUMMARY:National Strategic Review:
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20070207T160000
DESCRIPTION:AN INVESTMENT IN AUSTRALIA'S FUTURE:\nWHY THE MATHEMATICAL S
 CIENCES MATTER --\n7th FEBRUARY\n\nA Forum to discuss the National Strat
 egic Review\, conducted by the\nNational Committee for the Mathematical 
 Sciences\, will be held on\n7th February 2007\, 9.00am -- 4.00pm\, The S
 hine Dome\, Gordon Street\,\nCanberra.  This is a unique opportunity\, i
 n an election year and\nwhile Parliament is in session\, to draw attenti
 on to what the\nmathematical sciences can deliver for Australia\, and to
  draw\nattention to the substantial challenges facing mathematics and\ns
 tatistics. We strongly encourage mathematicians and statisticians\nto at
 tend to show support for our disciplines and this important event.\n\nTh
 e program for the forum will include speakers addressing Australia's\nre
 search enterprise in the mathematical sciences\, in the business\,\nindu
 stry\, government and university sectors.  Speakers will include\n Senat
 or Kim Carr\, Opposition spokesperson for industry and science\n Peter H
 aggstrom\, Deutsche Asset Management (Australia) Limited\n Peter Laver\,
  Director\, Australian Centre for Innovation and\n                      
          International Competitiveness\n John Rice\, Australian Council 
 of Deans\,\n Melanie Bahlo WEHI\n Frank de Hoog CSIRO
END:VEVENT
