LOCATION:Staff Club then E6A102
DTSTAMP:20071024T000422Z
UID:1BDAFFC1-FBA6-4CDC-B6DC-C65EEAFEFE9B
SEQUENCE:8
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20071029T000000
SUMMARY:Colloquium
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20071029T020000
DESCRIPTION:Mathematics  Colloquium\n\nDay:         Monday 29 October\n\
 nTime:               1 pm\n\nPlace:            E6A102\n\nSpeaker: Prof. 
 Robert Wisbauer\n              (Uni. of Duesseldorf)\n\nTitle: Reimporti
 ng category theory to module categories\n\nAbstract: The category of mod
 ules over an associative ring was one of the motivating examples to deve
 lop abstract category theories. Here new notions and relationships were 
 introduced and investigated which seemed to be going far beyond the  int
 erest of  ring theorists.  In this talk I  want to show that  many abstr
 act  notions can be brought back to module theory leading to new perspec
 tives and understanding.\n\n\n-----------------------------\nWe will tak
 e the speaker out to lunch at the Staff Club.  The lunch party departs f
 rom level 4 of E7A at noon.  Please join us.\n\n
END:VEVENT
