UID:89FF8114-39F5-41D6-8679-A8D2137F28C8
SEQUENCE:6
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20070331T193000
SUMMARY:Earth Hour
DESCRIPTION:Macquarie University is pleased to pledge its support to the
  World Wildlife Federation’s (WWF) Earth Hour\, in a bid to reduce green
 house emissions responsible for global warming.\n \nCommencing at 7.30pm
  and finishing at 8.30pm on Saturday 31 March 2007\, staff are requested
  to ensure all non-essential equipment is switched off\, including offic
 e\, classroom and laboratory lighting\, computers and especially their m
 onitors (not left on standby)\, and all office equipment which might nor
 mally be left on standby also.\n \nThe objective is to educate the commu
 nity about the threat of global warming\, and what each individual can d
 o in their day to day activities to reduce greenhouse emissions. The aim
  is to reduce Sydney’s emissions by 5% within a year following Earth Hou
 r\, primarily targeting electricity production and usage.\n \nThe Office
  of Facilities Management will be ensuring all non-essential building se
 rvices (eg. air conditioning) not required\, will be programmed not to o
 perate\, and Security will be switching off any lights inadvertently lef
 t on.  Due to OH&S   requirements\, the majority of external lighting wi
 ll remain on for this event.\n \nThe University’s participation in this 
 event\, is part of its community and environmental support of such initi
 atives.\n \nAdditional information can be found at www.earthhour.org
END:VEVENT
