SEQUENCE:7
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20080414T140000
SUMMARY:James Wallbridge
DESCRIPTION:	From: 	  james.wallbridge@adelaide.edu.au\n	Subject: 	Tanna
 ka project\n	Date: 	8 April 2008 11:25:47 PM\n	To: 	  street@ics.mq.edu.
 au\n\nDear Ross\,\n\nI am currently studying a PhD in Mathematics at the
  University of Adelaide (I recently began 2nd year).  I have been workin
 g for around 5 months on my own\nproject which is a higher categorical g
 eneralisation of Tannakian duality (the first paper I read on Tannaka th
 eory was by Joyal and yourself).  Much of that time however was spent at
  very interesting conferences.  In particular\, an advanced course at th
 e CRM in Barcelona where I had the pleasure of meeting Mark\nWeber\, amo
 ng others\, and two meetings at IAS Princeton where I was able to have d
 iscussions with Pierre Deligne.\n\nI have been invited to complete my Ph
 D (~2 years) in Toulouse with Bertrand Toen.  Unfortunately\, I have com
 e across some potential obstructions that hinder this opportunity.  I wa
 s wondering if I could organise a convenient time to call your office an
 d discuss my situation privately?  I would also like to ask about the po
 ssibility of spending some time later in the year at Maquarie to discuss
 \nmy research with Michael Batanin and yourself.\n\nBest regards\,\nJame
 s Wallbridge.\n\n
END:VEVENT
