BEGIN:VEVENT
DURATION:PT1H
LOCATION:E6A 133
DTSTAMP:20080512T020505Z
UID:B159409A-1202-4858-95A2-F2BF8E57DD1F
SEQUENCE:8
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20080512T130000
SUMMARY:Honours Talk
DESCRIPTION:Our Honours Students will be giving the first of their lectu
 res on\nMonday 5 May\nat 1 pm\nin E6A133\nA brief introduction to Lawver
 e theories\n\n\nMitchell Buckley\n \nAbstract\nBeginning with some basic
 s in Category Theory\, we outline the concepts of category\, functor and
  natural transformation. Following that we are able to define\nfunctor c
 ategories\; the morphisms here are natural transformations. Products of 
 objects will then be defined by a universal property. From these constru
 ctions\nalone\, we define what it means for a category to be a Bénabou o
 r Lawvere theory and move on to define their models (functors preserving
  finite products)\nand construct the category Mod(T\, Set) of models of 
 a Lawvere Theory T in Set. I will outline a few early propositions regar
 ding Mod(T\, Set) and finish by describing the usefulness of such an app
 roach in describing algebraic theories\nsuch as groups.\n\n
END:VEVENT
