UID:CFE16AAD-105C-4F6D-8B31-726819125884
SEQUENCE:4
DTSTAMP:20070402T235857Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DURATION:PT1H
LOCATION:Syd U\, Carslaw 373
DTSTAMP:20071015T025945Z
UID:D78B3D1F-DEEA-4F91-99C4-3F0156143023
SEQUENCE:5
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20071019T120000
SUMMARY:Algebra Seminar
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Daniel Murfet (Australian National University)\nDat
 e: Friday October 19\nTime: 12.05-12.55pm\nVenue: Carslaw 373\n\nTitle: 
 Homotopy categories\, Grothendieck duality and singularities\n\nAbstract
 :\nIt has been understood since the 1980s that there is a deep connectio
 n \nbetween finiteness conditions on categories of maximal Cohen-Macaula
 y \nmodules and the character of particular isolated singularities. This
  \ncan be understood in terms of stable module categories\, which are ni
 ce \nexamples of triangulated categories. Grothendieck duality describes
  \nan important property of another nice triangulated category\, the \nb
 ounded derived category of coherent sheaves on a projective variety. \nR
 ecent work involving compactly generated homotopy categories has given \
 nus new insight into both problems. I will talk about these developments
 \, \nincluding results from my PhD thesis.\n
END:VEVENT
