ATTENDEE;CN="Thomas Booker":invalid:nomail
LOCATION:E7B 161
DTSTAMP:20070813T043503Z
UID:8F826625-1EF0-4711-A4D6-7BCDDAE35B85
SEQUENCE:6
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20070816T140000
SUMMARY:Mathematics Honours 2nd round  Lecture
X-WR-ITIPSTATUSML:UNCLEAN
DESCRIPTION:Mathematics Honours 2nd round  Lecture\n\nTime: 2pm Thursday
  16 August 2007\n\nin E7B 161\n\nSpeaker: Thomas Booker\n\nTitle: Constr
 uctions in Topos Theory\nAbstract:\nHow does one have an analogy to the 
 natural numbers in a topos? What of the reals? What does it mean to take
  a Dedekind Cut in a topos-theoretic sense?\nI will also restate what it
  means for a category to be a topos.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
